# Repository-root ignores — keep credentials, editor state, and local-only
# tooling out of version control. (portal/ has its own .gitignore for the app.)

# Credentials — NEVER commit
key.json

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Dependencies (portal/ has its own ignore too; this guards the repo root)
node_modules/

# Test & tooling artifacts
.playwright-mcp/
# Local QA screenshots and scratch spreadsheets (manual e2e output; never committed)
e2e-*.png
*.xlsx

# CVE-remediation working artifacts — CLIENT VULNERABILITY DATA about a live system, and this
# repository is PUBLIC. `backend/scripts/exception_register.py map` writes these two by name
# into its --out-dir, and the row-level map is the most sensitive artifact in the whole pass:
# one line per finding, with package, version and installation path. `*.xlsx` above covers the
# incoming exports and the generated register; these are the formats that rule misses.
#
# Filename-only patterns match at any depth, so a relative --out-dir anywhere under the tree is
# covered. The working directory is supposed to live OUTSIDE the repo entirely — this is the
# backstop for the day somebody points --out-dir at `.`, not the control.
coverage-map.csv
coverage-summary.json
# `--overrides` input: per-CVE human commentary about a live client system — a dispute rationale
# or an accepted-risk note is MORE sensitive than the finding it annotates, not less.
overrides.json
# `*.xlsx` above misses the macro-enabled variant, which Excel writes whenever a workbook picks up
# a macro. Same bytes, same client data, one letter different.
*.xlsm

# OS
.DS_Store

# Local env (real secrets live in portal/.env, ignored there too)
.env
